keep art:compute-ledger
  where ~/.bonfyre/compute-ledger.sqlite3
  why rates DERIVED from real provider billing arithmetic, cross-validated exactly against the published book on 3 of 5 models; reconciles to the invoice within the web-search line item; 36 invariants
  caveat lives in the LEGACY path. Belongs under Aurekai's commerce/meter families.

keep art:partner-commons
  where ~/.bonfyre/partner-commons.sqlite3, 176 profiles, 1,885 authored role observations
  why the authored role assignments from the 82 deep-promotions and the family tables are real and were never in any state store
  caveat the 41 shipped repos supersede it as the definition of a partner. This is metadata ABOUT them.

keep art:cue-schemas
  where ~/Documents/Bonfyre/schemas/bonfyre.cue plus vet.sh
  why proven to reject: a promoted capability with proof_ref 'pending', an invariant with no reheat condition. Caught 15 uppercase capability names I had introduced.
  caveat schemas the legacy shape. Needs re-pointing at Aurekai's registry.

keep art:bonfyrequery-fix
  where ~/Documents/Bonfyre/cmd/BonfyreQuery/src/main.c
  why real defect, real fix, builds clean, stats returns 594 instead of a binder error
  action PORT UPSTREAM. The same bug is live at aurekai/native-runtime cmd/AkaiQuery/src/main.c:189. Fixing only the legacy copy is worthless.

delete art:local-generation-detour
  what the qwen2.5-3b gguf, the bonfyre-moe serve experiment, and the two invariants claiming local generation as a finding
  why it re-derived a documented forbidden_inference. foundry.yaff states it outright under burn: 'trained -> generation quality good (the FPQ lesson generalizes)'. tract already records the local execution phenotype as measured with a passing witness.
  cost two failed downloads, a filled root filesystem, a 30%-accuracy result
  ruling delete rather than record. A duplicate claim beside a witnessed original is worse than nothing.

delete art:native-sweep
  where ~/.bonfyre/native-sweep.sqlite3 and scratchpad/native_sweep.py
  why a hand-rolled capability prober written while bonfyre-capability and probe_native_capabilities.py both existed. The estate's prober names the exact defect in its own docstring.

review art:bonfyre-common
  where components/BonfyreControlPlane/bonfyre_common.py and bonfyre_common_equivalence.py
  status equivalence FAILED -- continuous_supervisor._iso(None) and verification._iso(None) return current time; four _parse variants reject whitespace while provider_state accepts it
  ruling correctly NOT migrated. Keep the harness, discard the premise that the family was one function.

review art:bonfyre-schema
  where components/BonfyreControlPlane/bonfyre_schema.py and bonfyre_schema_equivalence.py
  status codex verified GROUP_A 15/15, GROUP_B 6/6, DISAGREEMENTS NONE, SAFE_TO_MIGRATE
  scale the removal is worth ~15 lines; each body is 3 lines. The census counted copies, not code.
  ruling correct but low value. The finding that mattered was that the 15/6 split IS the foreign-key split.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ACTUALLY BLOCKS THE PRODUCT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

blocker anchor-bytepatch-skill
  status UNIMPLEMENTED, not missing
  what seven commands are declared hyper-delegated: anchor.build, anchor.lineage, bytepatch.emit, bytepatch.inspect, skill.run, skill.score, skill.tune
  evidence org-wide code search across all 49 aurekai repos returns NO hits for anchor.build, bytepatch or skill.run. No hyper.ts exists on disk anywhere.
  mechanism akai resolves AKAI_HYPER, then a compiled dist binary, then ../bonfyre-hyper/src/hyper.ts, then bare 'bonfyre-hyper' on PATH -- which is a symlink to akai.mjs itself, so it re-enters
  false_green pointing AKAI_HYPER at ANY executable flips akai runtime doctor from FAIL to PASS. It checks reachability, not capability. A stub would report health while all seven stay unimplemented.
  ruling these were declared and never written. That is the honest state.
